        "renderedText": "Tayfun SELEN · Member of the Board of County Commissioners\n\nRecords (11)\n\n“He immigrated to America in 1996, served as Mayor of Chatham Township, and is Senior Vice President of Administration for Lincoln Educational Services; a CPA.” — From the candidate's site — selenformorriscounty.com, read 2026-08-14\n\nFrom the candidate's site — selenformorriscounty.com, read 2026-08-14 · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nRecorded email: selentayfun@gmail.com\n\nMorris County Clerk · Read September 8th, 2026\n\nFiled mailing address: 30 Woodmont Drive Chatham NJ 07928\n\nMorris County Clerk, 2026 general-election candidate filing (read 2026-08-22) · Read August 22nd, 2026\n\nOfficial page: https://www.morriscountynj.gov/Departments/Board-of-County-Commissioners/Tayfun-Selen\n\nOfficial page · Read August 13th, 2026\n\nCampaign site: https://www.selenformorriscounty.com/\n\nCampaign site · Read August 22nd, 2026\n\nMember of the Board of County Commissioners appears on this ballot for 2026 General Election on November 3rd, 2026. Voters choose 1, for a term of 3 years.\n\nMorris County Clerk · Read September 8th, 2026\n\nTayfun SELEN filed for Member of the Board of County Commissioners, as Republican. The filing does not state whether they are the incumbent.\n\nMorris County Clerk · Read September 8th, 2026\n\nSearching Tayfun SELEN's published material for taxes found this passage: \"… Chatham Borough Zoning Board of Adjustment, and as a Chatham Township Committeeman and Mayor. As mayor, Commissioner Selen was responsible for reducing municipal property taxes, helping the township maintain a rare AAA credit rating, and reducing municipal spending by more than 10 percent. He also holds a seat on the Montclair State University …\"\n\nwww.morriscountynj.gov · Read August 20th, 2026\n\nSearching Tayfun SELEN's published material for taxes found this passage: \"… citizenship in 2008 and currently lives in Chatham Township with his wife and daughter. PROVEN CONSERVATIVE As a Mayor of Chatham Township, Tayfun cut municipal property taxes, earned a rare AAA credit rating, and reduced local spending by $200,000. PRIVATE SECTOR SUCCESS Professionally, Tayfun serves as Senior Vice President of Administration …\"\n\nwww.selenformorriscounty.com · Read August 20th, 2026\n\nTayfun Selen holds the office of County Commissioner, Republican.\n\nMorris County · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nSELEN, TAYFUN, 2026 election cycle: raised $225,025.50; spent $229,525.50. Filed with the New Jersey Election Law Enforcement Commission; read September 8th, 2026.\n\nNew Jersey Election Law Enforcement Commission · Read September 8th, 2026\n\nOur canonical officeholder records could not be read for this answer. This is a holding failure, not a finding that there are no officials for this place or person.\n\nWe have not recorded any actions in office for Tayfun Selen.\n\nWe have not established a canonical voting-office identity for Tayfun SELEN, so no other person's voting record has been attached.\n\nCounty filings: no applicable county filing was resolved for this answer about Tayfun SELEN. That does not establish that none exists.\n\nState filings: this answer uses the same state campaign-money records as the card. These records describe the campaigns' own filings; they do not establish outside spending for or against Tayfun SELEN.\n\nFederal filings: no applicable FEC record was resolved for this answer. This does not establish an absence of state or county filings.\n\nWho this is (9)\n\nSources: From the candidate's site — selenformorriscounty.com, read 2026-08-14, Morris County Clerk, Morris County Clerk, 2026 general-election candidate filing (read 2026-08-22), Official page, Campaign site, www.morriscountynj.gov, www.selenformorriscounty.com, Morris County, New Jersey Election Law Enforcement Commission",
