                "text": "BOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS MORRIS COUNTY, NEW JERSEY July 22, 2026 Regular Meeting Agenda TIME: 7:00 PM Generated 7/17/2026 4:56 PM This meeting is being held in person and livestreamed via WebEx. The public is invited to attend in person or to view the meeting by following the link below or by calling in to the phone number listed below the link. Public comments are welcome in person or by submitting written comments to the Clerk of the Board, which may be read or summarized during the public portion of the meeting. Written comments may be submitted via email with the subject line “Public Comment”’ to the Clerk of the Board, Michele Reilly at mreilly@co.morris.nj.us or by mail addressed to Michele Reilly, Clerk of the Board, Morris County Board of County Commissioners, PO Box 900, Morristown, NJ 07963-0900. Emailed comments must be received at least eight (8) hours prior to the meeting. Mailed comments must be received by 4:00 p.m. the day before the meeting. WebEx viewer link: https://morriscountynj.webex.com/morriscountynj/j.php?MTID=me17b12956292a6453524952e 56681c03 Webinar password : i5jChaRFM38 (45524273 when dialing from a phone or video system) Phone number: 1-408-418-9388 Event number/Access Code: 233 068 01695 ANNOUNCEMENT Adequate notice of this meeting held the 22nd day of July, 2026 has been provided through resolution adopted by this Board on January 2, 2026 at its Stated Annual Meeting held at the Administration and Records Building, Morristown, New Jersey and by electronic mailing to the Star Ledger and the Daily Record, through posting on the County website and by filing a copy of same with the Morris County Clerk and the Clerk of this Board. ROLL CALL Stephen H. Shaw Director John Krickus Deputy Director Douglas R. Cabana Thomas J. Mastrangelo Christine Myers Tayfun Selen Deborah Smith OTHERS PRESENT Deena Leary, County Administrator; Brian Murray, Assistant County Administrator; John Napolitano, County Counsel; Staci Santucci, Assistant County Counsel; Michele Reilly, Clerk of the Board\nJULY 22, 2026 REGULAR COMMISSIONER MEETING 2 | P a g e PRAYER AND FLAG SALUTE PRESENTATION MINUTES FOR APPROVAL July 8, 2026, Work Session Meeting Minutes and Regular Meeting Minutes Action Taken: COMMUNICATIONS 1. The Town of Boonton is requesting permission, on behalf of the Boonton Fire Department, to close portions of Main Street (CR 511, CR 624), West Main Street (CR 624), and Washington Street/Route 202 (CR 511) between Lake Avenue and Grant Street on Saturday, September 5, 2026 (rain date: Monday, September 7, 2026), for the Labor Day Parade from 12:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. 2. The Hilltop Christian Nursery School is requesting permission to hang a banner over Main Street/Route 24 (CR 510) in Mendham Borough from July 27, 2026 to July 31, 2026 advertise that the Hilltop Christian Nursery School registration is open. 3. DJB Event Consultants, Inc. is requesting permission to use a portion of Washington Street (CR 510) between Conklin Avenue and Colonial Road, and Sussex Avenue (CR 617) between Mill Street and Elliot Street, Morristown for the Morristown Corporate Classic 5K Run for JWBS on Thursday, July 23, 2026, from 6:00 p.m. to 9:30 p.m. Action Taken: ORDINANCES: First Reading/Introduction ORDINANCES: Second Reading/Public Hearing OPEN TO THE PUBLIC RESOLUTIONS Action Taken: PAYMENT OF BILLS Action Taken: COMMISSIONER COMMENTS ADJOURNMENT\nJULY 22, 2026 REGULAR COMMISSIONER MEETING 3 | P a g e REGULAR COMMISSIONER MEETING RESOLUTIONS RES-2026-576. Resolution Authorizing the Commissioner Director to Execute an Amendment to Historic Preservation Easement between the Township of Pequannock and The County of Morris, for a 30-year deed restriction and protection for the preservation work at the Pompton Plains Railroad Station which was assisted by grants from the Open Space, Recreation, Farmland and Historic Preservation Trust (Office of Planning & Preservation) (ID #14222) RES-2026-577. Resolution Authorizing the County Chief Financial Officer to issue checks per Chapter 127 P.L. 1985 (Department of Finance) (ID #14217) RES-2026-578. Resolution Authorizing the County Chief Financial Officer to reissue check(s) that has/have been lost and payment has/have been stopped (Department of Finance) (ID #14220) RES-2026-579. Resolution Authorizing the Application and Award of the Local Public Health Infrastructure Grant in the amount of $119,372.00 (Department of Law & Public Safety) (ID #14223) RES-2026-580. Resolution Authorizing the Acceptance of the Grant Award for the Overdose Fatality Review Teams Grant for FY27 in the amount of $75,000.00 (Department of Law & Public Safety) (ID #14224) RES-2026-581. Resolution Authorizing an Award of a Contract to TENEX Software Solutions, Inc. for upgrades and maintenance of proprietary hardware, software, and equipment a total not to exceed expenditure of $27,250.00 (Purchasing) (ID #14216) RES-2026-582. Resolution Authorizing the County Chief Financial Officer to Reclassify Payments from One Account to Another (Department of Finance) (ID #14234) RES-2026-583. Resolution Authorizing the Sale of a 1994 Pierce Lance Pumper (VIN 4P1CT02S2RA000549) to the Jersey City Fire Department (Department of Law & Public Safety) (ID #14236) RES-2026-584. Resolution Authorizing Approval of the Right of Way License and Hold Harmless Agreement between the County of Morris and the Township of Denville for property located in Denville (County Counsel) (ID #14246) RES-2026-585. Resolution Authorizing Payment to the Bank of America through the County's PCARD program, in the amount of $12.45 (Department of Finance) (ID #14225) RES-2026-586. Resolution to Reclassify a Total of $120,929.15 in WIOA Youth Expenditures from FY26 to FY25 (Office of Planning & Preservation) (ID #14237) RES-2026-587. Resolution Authorizing an Increase under the State of New Jersey Office of Homeland Security and Preparedness FFY 2026 C-UASGP - State Share for a new grant total of $9,961,060.00. (Department of Law & Public Safety) (ID #14239) RES-2026-588. Resolution to Award a Non-fair and Open Contract for the Provision of Proprietary Software & Licensing to TENEX Software Solutions, Inc. to provide TENEX Precinct Central & ExpressLink Integration Proprietary Software & Licensing for $131,375.00 from October 1, 2026 through September 30, 2027 (Purchasing) (ID #14241)\nJULY 22, 2026 REGULAR COMMISSIONER MEETING 4 | P a g e RES-2026-589. Resolution Awarding a Contract for Bid #M25-37 Milling & Resurfacing, Sussex Turnpike (C.R. 617), Township of Randolph to Riverview Paving, Inc. for the amount of $1,371,613.62 (Department of Public Works) (ID #14243) RES-2026-590. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Transportation, Upgrade Railroad Crossing Surface – Union Street, in the amount of $178,370.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14229) RES-2026-591. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Community Affairs, Universal Service Fund (USF) CWA Admin 2026, in the amount of $3,844.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14230) RES-2026-592. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Community Affairs, Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program (LIHEAP) CWA Admin 2026, in the amount of $6,013.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14231) RES-2026-593. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Law and Public Safety, State Facilities Education Act (SFEA) 2026-2027, in the amount of $47,280.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14232) RES-2026-594. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Health, Disaster Preparedness, Resiliency, and Emergency Medical Services (DPREMS), in the amount of $301,813.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14233) RES-2026-595. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Human Services, Work First New Jersey, in the amount of $473,074.00 (Department of Finance) (ID #14235) RES-2026-596. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Transportation, Indian Falls Road Bridge No. 1400-992, in the amount of $47,834.39 (Department of Finance) (ID #14240) RES-2026-597. Resolution Accepting Additional NJDOT Grant Funding in the Amount of $393,558.26 for the Replacement of County Bridge No. 1400-992 on Indian Falls Road over Jackson Brook in the Township of Mine Hill, County of Morris (Department of Public Works) (ID #14244) RES-2026-598. Resolution Authorizing the Insertion of a Special Item of Revenue into the 2026 Budget under Chapter 159, New Jersey Department of Transportation, Indian Falls Road Bridge No. 1400-992, in the amount of $393,558.26 (Department of Finance) (ID #14245) RES-2026-599. Resolution Authorizing the Submission of the 2026 Annual Action Plan (Department of Human Services) (ID #14226) RES-2026-600. Resolution Authorizing Anticipated Program Income Funds to be Funded Under the Housing Rehabilitation Program and Other CDBG Projects (Department of Human Services) (ID #14227) RES-2026-601. Resolution Authorizing Anticipated HOME Program Income and Recaptured funds to be allotted for eligible HOME Program activities (Department of Human Services) (ID #14228)\nJULY 22, 2026 REGULAR COMMISSIONER MEETING 5 | P a g e RES-2026-602. Resolution Authorizing Award of Contract for Bid # B26-111 As-Needed Traffic Signal and Electrician Services for Morris County Owned Traffic Signals to Jen Electric for $23,600.00 (Department of Public Works) (ID #14242) RES-2026-603. Resolution to Approve Renewal 