            "topic": "income-tax",
            "question": "Is there a state income tax?",
            "answer": "No — New Hampshire does not tax wages, and its separate tax on interest and dividends was repealed effective 2025. There is also no state sales tax.",
            "sourceUrl": "https://www.revenue.nh.gov/",
            "sourceOrg": "New Hampshire Department of Revenue Administration",
