          {
            "topic": "property-tax",
            "question": "How do property taxes work?",
            "answer": "Property taxes are the main way New Hampshire towns and schools are funded, set town by town; the annual town meeting votes the budget that drives the rate. Credits and exemptions (veterans, elderly, disabled) run through your town.",
            "sourceUrl": "https://www.revenue.nh.gov/",
