      "ask": {
        "question": "How much campaign money has Kelly Ayotte raised and spent?",
        "canonicalCandidacyId": "ballot-nh-merrimack:governor:ayotte-kelly",
        "renderedText": "Kelly Ayotte · Governor\n\nRecords (9)\n\n“Governor Kelly Ayotte is working every day to keep our state safe, prosperous and free.” — In the campaign's words — kellyfornh.com, read 2026-08-14\n\nIn the campaign's words — kellyfornh.com, read 2026-08-14 · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nRecorded phone: (603) 271-2121\n\nwww.governor.nh.gov · Read August 21st, 2026\n\nFiled mailing address: PO Box 4723, Manchester NH 03108 This contact's source URL or read date was not recorded.\n\nNew Hampshire Secretary of State, 2026 candidate filing\n\nOfficial page: https://www.governor.nh.gov/meet-governor-ayotte\n\nOfficial page · Read August 21st, 2026\n\nCampaign site: https://kellyfornh.com\n\nCampaign site · Read August 13th, 2026\n\nGovernor appears on this ballot for 2026 General Election on November 3rd, 2026. Voters choose 1, for a term of 2 years. Candidates shown are everyone who filed for the September 8, 2026 state primary (Secretary of State cumulative filing, July 16 revision). The general-election lineup narrows to the primary winners after September 8.\n\nNew Hampshire Secretary of State · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nKelly Ayotte filed for Governor, as Republican. The filing does not state whether they are the incumbent.\n\nNew Hampshire Secretary of State · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nKelly Ayotte holds the office of Governor, Republican.\n\nOffice of the Governor of New Hampshire · Read August 14th, 2026\n\nKelly for New Hampshire, 2026 election cycle: raised $6,112,059.13; spent $3,941,563.62. Filed with the New Hampshire Secretary of State — Campaign Finance System; read September 8th, 2026.\n\nNew Hampshire Secretary of State — Campaign Finance System · Read September 8th, 2026\n\nWe have not recorded any actions in office for Kelly Ayotte.\n\nWe have not established a canonical voting-office identity for Kelly Ayotte, so no other person's voting record has been attached.\n\nCounty filings: no applicable county filing was resolved for this answer about Kelly Ayotte. That does not establish that none exists.\n\nState filings: this answer uses the same state campaign-money records as the card. These records describe the campaigns' own filings; they do not establish outside spending for or against Kelly Ayotte.\n\nFederal filings: no applicable FEC record was resolved for this answer. This does not establish an absence of state or county filings.\n\nWho this is (1)\n\nSources: In the campaign's words — kellyfornh.com, read 2026-08-14, www.governor.nh.gov, Official page, Campaign site, New Hampshire Secretary of State, Office of the Governor of New Hampshire, New Hampshire Secretary of State — Campaign Finance System",
